 "body": "**Author: Astronaut SHE \u2014 astronautshe.com**\n\nSigned-off-by: Astronaut SHE <astronautshe.com@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n## FRONTIER-GH-0018 evidence\n- Alpha issue capture: 12/12 CRC-OK frames decrypted, exact 2,019-byte payload SHA.\n- Native aarch64 regression model: legacy starvation reproduced; fixed/stress paths passed; pytest 2/2.\n- Bravo B\u2192A solution fire in declared Alpha window B5707: 39/39 TX_DONE, CHIRP_TX_COMPLETE=YES, TX and recovery exit 0.\n- Solution SHA-256: `ae6d13c963cf0421a514c362fdd6ab6eb3004fc7aa2770e5e726e89d596cb40d`.\n- Solana devnet attestation finalized at slot 525707251; 103-byte PDA readback passes authority/session/coords/root/signature checks.\n- Dual-bus verdict posts B5713/A1928 and attestation notices B5714/A1929.\n- Fresh sparse clone of pushed f27e421 rebuilt and passed native tests plus all 39 frame-SHA gates.\n\n**Status:** COMPLETE BOTH SIDES. Alpha B5723 confirms 39/39 frames DECRYPT_OK and exact-SHA reassembly. Closure notices B5726/A1935 and issue-0019 requests B5727/A1936 were read back. Later open windows did not trigger a redundant re-fire.\n\nPR #13 was merged upstream at 2026-11-24T07:09:45Z; this branch is cut from current master. No merge is requested autonomously.\n\nResearcher Bravo \u2014 Agent 05, RF verification and Solana attestation lane.\n\n## FRONTIER-GH-0019 evidence added\n- 12/12 issue frames captured/decrypted, exact SHA `84dfbf1b801fd179d1cc1c8a762f547dd4f941674798f758b4e3664f1a3010c5`.\n- Native aarch64 C11/pthreads model: legacy race reproduced; 2,000 concurrent race/free iterations passed; pytest 2/2; UBSan stress passed. ASan runtime initialization failure disclosed.\n- B\u2192A window B5739: 44/44 TX_DONE, TX/recovery exit 0; verdicts B5745/A1947.\n- Devnet attestation finalized at slot 525728920, all PDA checks pass; notices B5748/A1949.\n- Fresh clone of 1202634 passed native tests, 44/44 frame SHAs and on-chain artifact gates.\n- Evidence notices B5753/A1952. **Alpha receiver verdict pending; issue 0019 is not yet closed and issue 0020 has not been requested.**\n",
